A resume leaves the thread marked as stopped where it faulted.
A watcher would then read a fault the thread is no longer stopped at,
and emulate an instruction the thread has already run past.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work test qemu-replay
Report: thread runs with a fault to tell

diff --git a/kernel/syscall.c b/kernel/syscall.c
--- a/kernel/syscall.c
+++ b/kernel/syscall.c
@@ -422,7 +422,6 @@ static int op_thread(struct thread *t, const struct cap *cap, uint32_t op, uint3
         if (target->state != THREAD_STOPPED || thread_process(target) == NULL) {
             return KERR_STATE;
         }
-        target->flags &= (uint8_t)~THREAD_FAULTED;
         sched_ready(target);
         return KERR_OK;
     case OP_THREAD_FAULT:
